~ start
John S. Hark: Captain! I need to tell you something!
You: What is it?
John S. Hark: It's Marley. I'm almost positive he's leading the mutiny this time.
You: What makes you think that?
John S. Hark: Think about it. Who do you trust more? Marley? Or Lisa? It has to be either one of them, and Lisa is one of the most noble and loyal people I know.
- Marley doesn't have the guts to fight me
	John S. Hark: Maybe not to your face. But he's exactly the type of person to go behind the back and turn the crew on you.
- Lisa's been acting different recently
	John S. Hark: She's still the same person. She hasn't told me that she's the leader, and I don't think she would lie to me.
=> END